## 2026-09-26 — Keep the session on point without discarding side questions

Development-main closeout (not an installed-runtime claim): ask what moves the current therapeutic focus forward; judge side-ness by relevance, so an apparently side question that bears on the target is pursued. Park real side questions with why they might matter, and bring one back when the focus allows: hold while the focus is urgent, mention one briefly when an important one has waited or several are waiting, and let it become the main question once the focus is light. When the client drifts, acknowledge the topic warmly, save it, and return to the focus. A client's theory of what a symptom protects against is tested only when the answer would change the next step. Separately, the owner confirmed that suicidal_state deliberately does not escalate the processing tier or add generic crisis copy.

Authority and evidence: owner decisions of 2026-09-26 in `tasks/focus-discipline-20260926/OWNER-DECISIONS.json`; `tests/focus-discipline*.test.mjs` and `tests/owner-decision-suicidal-state.test.mjs`. Scripted trajectories are not live or clinical results.

